{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circular piece of metal of maximum size is cut out of a square piece and then a square piece of maximum size is cut out of the circular piece. The total amount of metal wasted is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872355e2143d0a95793f42e46d0e6e2e09d5b348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ the area of the original square}\\\\  \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\text{ the area of the original square}\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\text{ the area of the circular piece}\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\text{ the area of the circular piece}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"169\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The maximum diameter of the circular piece is the same as the side length of the square piece, so the circle is tangent to the square on all four sides. The maximum size a square piece that you can cut from the circle now has 4 edges that are the same as the square created by connecting the four midpoints of the original square. If the side length of the original square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, then the sides of the final square have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/9074d6d5ff009844996684639cc35b1d7188a56d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{s^2}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"43\" />, so its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a4cc7461bb1002b26875b47b5f152c546b25882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> the area of the original square. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width